    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n44084" root="&#xA;                        نفق&#xA;                    " body-key="n1">
                        
                            <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">نَفَقٌ</span></b> 
                        : see <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">سَرَبٌ</span> ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَنْفَاقٌ</span> The <i>hole</i> of rats
or mice. (S, TA in art. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">خفى</span>:) see 1 in that
art.: <i>holes in the ground;</i> or <i>subterranean
excavations</i> or <i>habitations;</i> pl. of <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">نَفَقٌ</span>. (TA
in art. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">دسم</span>.) See 5. ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A2-  Also <i>Fresh olive-oil:</i>
see <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فَاقٌ</span> in art. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فوق</span>: also mentioned in art. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">نفق</span>
in the TA.

